        {
          "id": "p_ch25_029",
          "text": "I’ve got seven years under my belt, so I’m safe. Bhatia can’t force me to take the buyout. But his message about my future at the Detroit Free Press is clear.",
          "html": "I’ve got seven years under my belt, so I’m safe. Bhatia can’t force me to take the buyout. But his message about my future at the <em>Detroit</em> <em>Free Press</em> is clear.",
          "word_count": 31
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_030",
          "text": "I stand up and numbly shake hands all around. My face is flushing as I stumble out of the newsroom, feeling like I’ve been hit with a flash-bang grenade.",
          "html": "I stand up and numbly shake hands all around. My face is flushing as I stumble out of the newsroom, feeling like I’ve been hit with a flash-bang grenade.",
          "word_count": 29
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_031",
          "text": "Hours later, still reeling from the meeting, I receive a phone call from Willie Horton—one of the organization’s legendary figures. Earlier this off-season, he called, suggesting we meet sometime soon.",
          "html": "Hours later, still reeling from the meeting, I receive a phone call from Willie Horton—one of the organization’s legendary figures. Earlier this off-season, he called, suggesting we meet sometime soon.",
          "word_count": 30
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_032",
          "text": "His timing prompts me to wonder: Has he somehow heard about today’s meeting?",
          "html": "His timing prompts me to wonder: Has he somehow heard about today’s meeting?",
          "word_count": 13
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_033",
          "text": "He doesn’t mention it. Neither do I. He invites me over to his house tomorrow and I accept eagerly. We hang out in his basement museum—signed baseballs, photographs, plaques, a wood-carved figurine of Tiger Stadium.",
          "html": "He doesn’t mention it. Neither do I. He invites me over to his house tomorrow and I accept eagerly. We hang out in his basement museum—signed baseballs, photographs, plaques, a wood-carved figurine of Tiger Stadium.",
          "word_count": 35
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_034",
          "text": "After nearly two hours, he passes over a folder of hitting strategies and an email report he sent directly to the Highest Source In The Land. Before I go, I’m introduced to one of his daughters.",
          "html": "After nearly two hours, he passes over a folder of hitting strategies and an email report he sent directly to the Highest Source In The Land. Before I go, I’m introduced to one of his daughters.",
          "word_count": 36
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_035",
          "text": "I message my closest work confidante: “On the day they told me they didn’t want me covering the Tigers anymore, I broke a trade and received a call from Willie Horton, inviting me to his house.”",
          "html": "I message my closest work confidante: “On the day they told me they didn’t want me covering the Tigers anymore, I broke a trade and received a call from Willie Horton, inviting me to his house.”",
          "word_count": 36
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_036",
          "text": "SAN DIEGO, December 8—The Winter Meetings again. Perhaps, for me, the final one—a scary thought I cannot shake. It is raining as I arrive at the Manchester Grand Hyatt Resort.",
          "html": "SAN DIEGO, <em>December 8</em>—The Winter Meetings again. Perhaps, for me, the final one—a scary thought I cannot shake. It is raining as I arrive at the Manchester Grand Hyatt Resort.",
          "word_count": 30
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_037",
          "text": "I can still see my first day ever at the Ball Writing carnival. I remember pulling out my wallet to make sure I had at least five business cards packed into the outside flap.",
          "html": "I can still see my first day ever at the Ball Writing carnival. I remember pulling out my wallet to make sure I had at least five business cards packed into the outside flap.",
          "word_count": 34
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_038",
          "text": "Today, I have none. I don’t even have a back pocket. I’m wearing sweats. Waiting for the elevator, I run into an Arizona reporter. When we return from lunch, Kristie Ackert is at the sports bar. Dylan Hernández is here somewhere. The whole gang.",
          "html": "Today, I have none. I don’t even have a back pocket. I’m wearing sweats. Waiting for the elevator, I run into an Arizona reporter. When we return from lunch, Kristie Ackert is at the sports bar. Dylan Hernández is here somewhere. The whole gang.",
          "word_count": 44
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_039",
          "text": "There’s no Tigers-oriented celebration this year. Second baseman Lou Whitaker is not elected to the Hall of Fame by the veterans’ committee, as double-play partner Alan Trammell was last year. Sweet Lou was selected on 6 of 16 ballots, falling short of the 12 required for election. I didn’t even bother to pre-write a story—Whitaker’s been getting screwed for years.",
          "html": "There’s no Tigers-oriented celebration this year. Second baseman Lou Whitaker is not elected to the Hall of Fame by the veterans’ committee, as double-play partner Alan Trammell was last year. Sweet Lou was selected on 6 of 16 ballots, falling short of the 12 required for election. I didn’t even bother to pre-write a story—Whitaker’s been getting screwed for years.",
          "word_count": 60
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_040",
          "text": "I’m here as a lame duck, a hawk whose wings have been clipped. Only a select few know how my career hangs by a thread, but everyone knows who I am—the unethical guy who Justin Verlander doesn’t like.",
          "html": "I’m here as a lame duck, a hawk whose wings have been clipped. Only a select few know how my career hangs by a thread, but everyone knows who I am—the unethical guy who Justin Verlander doesn’t like.",
          "word_count": 38
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_041",
          "text": "Five years ago, this was still a dream. I hadn’t the earthliest clue of how to get scoops. A simpler time. Just happy to be here, closing the lobby bar each night, meeting new people all the time.",
          "html": "Five years ago, this was still a dream. I hadn’t the earthliest clue of how to get scoops. A simpler time. Just happy to be here, closing the lobby bar each night, meeting new people all the time.",
          "word_count": 38
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_042",
          "text": "Tonight, I go to my room after dinner. Take a sleeping pill. In bed by 11.",
          "html": "Tonight, I go to my room after dinner. Take a sleeping pill. In bed by 11.",
          "word_count": 16
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_043",
          "text": "December 9—The last thing I want to do is linger at the lobby bar for familiar faces. As expected, everybody asks about the Verlander thing. It’s frustrating because it’s not something I can explain in one standing conversation. Not something I particularly want to explain.",
          "html": "<em>December 9</em>—The last thing I want to do is linger at the lobby bar for familiar faces. As expected, everybody asks about the Verlander thing. It’s frustrating because it’s not something I can explain in one standing conversation. Not something I particularly want to explain.",
          "word_count": 45
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_044",
          "text": "Reporting-wise, I’m in a tight spot. Aware of my impending assignment change, Al Avila and other officers have no incentive to help me. The last thing they want is the Free Press getting cold feet about re-assigning me. I’ve become an annoying, truth-telling pest.",
          "html": "Reporting-wise, I’m in a tight spot. Aware of my impending assignment change, Al Avila and other officers have no incentive to help me. The last thing they want is the <em>Free Press</em> getting cold feet about re-assigning me. I’ve become an annoying, truth-telling pest.",
          "word_count": 44
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_045",
          "text": "Not only that, but Deep Throat isn’t here this year. Vacationing somewhere tropical. Might not even be in the country, I can’t remember.",
          "html": "Not only that, but Deep Throat isn’t here this year. Vacationing somewhere tropical. Might not even be in the country, I can’t remember.",
          "word_count": 23
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_046",
          "text": "“Are you still in the loop of things going down?”",
          "html": "“Are you still in the loop of things going down?”",
          "word_count": 10
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_047",
          "text": "“No.”",
          "html": "“No.”",
          "word_count": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_048",
          "text": "I lay low in my room. When I see someone I know on the floor, my first instinct is to walk the other way. I haven’t aggressively sought out info from sources.",
          "html": "I lay low in my room. When I see someone I know on the floor, my first instinct is to walk the other way. I haven’t aggressively sought out info from sources.",
          "word_count": 32
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_049",
          "text": "Unlike five years ago, I know nearly all the agents, but I haven’t reached out to many this offseason… can’t remember the last time I opened ScoopSheet.",
          "html": "Unlike five years ago, I know nearly all the agents, but I haven’t reached out to many this offseason… can’t remember the last time I opened ScoopSheet.",
          "word_count": 27
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_050",
          "text": "Jim Leyland still wanders around the winter meetings like he did back then, looking for restaurants the way teenagers look at mall directories—lost. Leyland is looking for lunch when we cross paths. He asks if I’m hungry. “Wanna join?”",
          "html": "Jim Leyland still wanders around the winter meetings like he did back then, looking for restaurants the way teenagers look at mall directories—lost. Leyland is looking for lunch when we cross paths. He asks if I’m hungry. “Wanna join?”",
          "word_count": 39
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_051",
          "text": "We sit at a white-table Italian spot. First topic is Lou Whitaker’s Hall of Fame candidacy. Leyland managed Whitaker in his first full season in the minor leagues in 1976 at Class A Lakeland. Whitaker was 19. Two years later, he’d win Rookie of the Year.",
          "html": "We sit at a white-table Italian spot. First topic is Lou Whitaker’s Hall of Fame candidacy. Leyland managed Whitaker in his first full season in the minor leagues in 1976 at Class A Lakeland. Whitaker was 19. Two years later, he’d win Rookie of the Year.",
          "word_count": 46
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_052",
          "text": "I ask Leyland if he thinks Whitaker is a Hall of Famer.",
          "html": "I ask Leyland if he thinks Whitaker is a Hall of Famer.",
          "word_count": 12
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_053",
          "text": "“I do… I do.”",
          "html": "“I do… I do.”",
          "word_count": 4
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_054",
          "text": "“Do you think he’ll get in eventually?”",
          "html": "“Do you think he’ll get in eventually?”",
          "word_count": 7
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_055",
          "text": "“I do… I do.”",
          "html": "“I do… I do.”",
          "word_count": 4
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_056",
          "text": "Leyland will eventually be canonized in Cooperstown himself. As with all managers and executives, Leyland was voted in by the veterans’ committee and inducted in July 2024.",
          "html": "Leyland will eventually be canonized in Cooperstown himself. As with all managers and executives, Leyland was voted in by the veterans’ committee and inducted in July 2024.",
          "word_count": 27
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_057",
          "text": "The waitress asks about Leyland’s shiny ring—he’s wearing his 2012 American League championship ring.",
          "html": "The waitress asks about Leyland’s shiny ring—he’s wearing his 2012 American League championship ring.",
          "word_count": 14
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_058",
          "text": "“I never wear any of them, but when I come to the meetings, sometimes people like to see ‘em. So, I just picked this one.”",
          "html": "“I never wear any of them, but when I come to the meetings, sometimes people like to see ‘em. So, I just picked this one.”",
          "word_count": 25
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_059",
          "text": "He says he’s won 12-to-14 rings between the minors and majors.",
          "html": "He says he’s won 12-to-14 rings between the minors and majors.",
          "word_count": 11
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_060",
          "text": "“You can have it if you want it.”",
          "html": "“You can have it if you want it.”",
          "word_count": 8
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_061",
          "text": "“Really?!” she laughs.",
          "html": "“Really?!” she laughs.",
          "word_count": 3
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_062",
          "text": "More folks walk up.",
          "html": "More folks walk up.",
          "word_count": 4
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_063",
          "text": "Braves manager Brian Snitker is joined by Jonathan Schuerholz, the son of Hall of Fame executive John Schuerholz.",
          "html": "Braves manager Brian Snitker is joined by Jonathan Schuerholz, the son of Hall of Fame executive John Schuerholz.",
          "word_count": 18
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_064",
          "text": "“He’s a good manager,” Leyland says of Snitker. “He paid his price.”",
          "html": "“He’s a good manager,” Leyland says of Snitker. “He paid his price.”",
          "word_count": 12
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_065",
          "text": "Snitker’s minor-league tour of duty makes Leyland’s 11 years seem short—Snitker, 64, managed 20 minor-league seasons before debuting in the majors in 2016.",
          "html": "Snitker’s minor-league tour of duty makes Leyland’s 11 years seem short—Snitker, 64, managed 20 minor-league seasons before debuting in the majors in 2016.",
          "word_count": 23
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_066",
          "text": "Over a quick snack, I ask Leyland about managing and the benefit of minor-league experience.",
          "html": "Over a quick snack, I ask Leyland about managing and the benefit of minor-league experience.",
          "word_count": 15
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_067",
          "text": "“It’s like with anything… You’ve seen that movie before. When a situation comes up, you’ve seen it before.”",
          "html": "“It’s like with anything… You’ve seen that movie before. When a situation comes up, you’ve seen it before.”",
          "word_count": 18
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_068",
          "text": "He likes the younger crop of guys, but he laments his generation hasn’t gotten more chances, too.",
          "html": "He likes the younger crop of guys, but he laments his generation hasn’t gotten more chances, too.",
          "word_count": 17
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_069",
          "text": "“I’d just rather see guys like myself get a chance from a selfish standpoint. Guys that have paid their dues.”",
          "html": "“I’d just rather see guys like myself get a chance from a selfish standpoint. Guys that have paid their dues.”",
          "word_count": 20
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_070",
          "text": "Lunch is quick. I got a pasta starter and a glass of white wine. He got a sandwich, no wine. Despite pleas that the Free Press can afford it, Leyland picks up the tab. I don’t know if he knows what’s going on with me, or if we just happened to bump into each other in the right place at the right time.",
          "html": "Lunch is quick. I got a pasta starter and a glass of white wine. He got a sandwich, no wine. Despite pleas that the <em>Free Press</em> can afford it, Leyland picks up the tab. I don’t know if he knows what’s going on with me, or if we just happened to bump into each other in the right place at the right time.",
          "word_count": 63
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_071",
          "text": "Walking back to the hotel, we run into a couple of Tigers Guys and stop to say hello. Leyland points at me.",
          "html": "Walking back to the hotel, we run into a couple of Tigers Guys and stop to say hello. Leyland points at me.",
          "word_count": 22
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_072",
          "text": "“He’s ripping somebody today. You know that.”",
          "html": "“He’s ripping somebody today. You know that.”",
          "word_count": 7
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_073",
          "text": "Leyland is prophetic. Turns out that The Highest Source In The Land is selling today—and I’m not buying.",
          "html": "Leyland is prophetic. Turns out that The Highest Source In The Land is selling today—and I’m not buying.",
          "word_count": 18
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_074",
          "text": "Sounding like a robot programmed to parrot buzz-phrases, Al Avila talks about “building it up” at his first media session of the week inside the team’s suite. Avila uses some variation of the phrase seven times in 37 minutes.",
          "html": "Sounding like a robot programmed to parrot buzz-phrases, Al Avila talks about “building it up” at his first media session of the week inside the team’s suite. Avila uses some variation of the phrase seven times in 37 minutes.",
          "word_count": 39
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_075",
          "text": "I comment to a colleague: “Five bucks says he was coached to say that.”",
          "html": "I comment to a colleague: “Five bucks says he was coached to say that.”",
          "word_count": 14
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_076",
          "text": "“I have absolutely no doubt.”",
          "html": "“I have absolutely no doubt.”",
          "word_count": 5
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_077",
          "text": "I write a column critical of the approach, calling out the Propaganda Police:",
          "html": "I write a column critical of the approach, calling out the Propaganda Police:",
          "word_count": 13
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_078",
          "text": "“The Tigers wanted Avila to deliver optimism—they sense fans’ frustration reaching a boil. They know confidence is at an all-time low.",
          "html": "“The Tigers wanted Avila to deliver optimism—they sense fans’ frustration reaching a boil. They know confidence is at an all-time low.",
          "word_count": 21
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_079",
          "text": "“Instead, he offered words he can’t back up: The message of a team ready to turn the page, of having money to spend, inching ever closer, and excitement—a message that sounds like the start of the process. Back then, it was a ‘retool,’ not a ‘rebuild.’",
          "html": "“Instead, he offered words he can’t back up: The message of a team ready to turn the page, of having money to spend, inching ever closer, and excitement—a message that sounds like the start of the process. Back then, it was a ‘retool,’ not a ‘rebuild.’",
          "word_count": 46
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_080",
          "text": "“It’s more lip service than substance. They’re good at delivering buzz phrases.”",
          "html": "“It’s more lip service than substance. They’re good at delivering buzz phrases.”",
          "word_count": 12
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_081",
          "text": "December 10—I work from my room today until the Tigers media availability at 4:30, when I decide to raise hell again.",
          "html": "<em>December 10</em>—I work from my room today until the Tigers media availability at 4:30, when I decide to raise hell again.",
          "word_count": 21
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_082",
          "text": "Al Avila sits flanked by manager Ron Gardenhire and VP of player development Dave Littlefield. They drone on about analytics and the minor leagues before I jump in.",
          "html": "Al Avila sits flanked by manager Ron Gardenhire and VP of player development Dave Littlefield. They drone on about analytics and the minor leagues before I jump in.",
          "word_count": 28
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_083",
          "text": "“Four years ago, I think it was in Nashville, you said you were going to come up with the ‘Tiger Way’ plan. Kind of like a uniform plan for players to play the game…”",
          "html": "“Four years ago, I think it was in Nashville, you said you were going to come up with the ‘Tiger Way’ plan. Kind of like a uniform plan for players to play the game…”",
          "word_count": 34
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_084",
          "text": "“We have a manual. It started with Tram, and Sam (Menzin) is the one that put it together.”",
          "html": "“We have a manual. It started with Tram, and Sam (Menzin) is the one that put it together.”",
          "word_count": 18
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_085",
          "text": "I’ve been poking around about this Tiger Way thing, and guys across the minors haven’t even heard of it. I ask Al to describe it.",
          "html": "I’ve been poking around about this Tiger Way thing, and guys across the minors haven’t even heard of it. I ask Al to describe it.",
          "word_count": 25
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_086",
          "text": "“Well, there’s a lot to that, to just make a comment. And you can fill in the blanks a lot of different ways, but we want our players, obviously, to play the game the right way. Obviously, we want the hustle, we want the fundamentals, things of that nature. So, when you look at the Tiger Way, it’s running the bases, defensive situations, knowing where to set up, where to hit the cut-off man, things of that nature. It’s no different than the Dodger Way when I grew up. It showed you where you’re supposed to be set up on almost every play defensively and how you’re supposed to approach certain situations.",
          "html": "“Well, there’s a lot to that, to just make a comment. And you can fill in the blanks a lot of different ways, but we want our players, obviously, to play the game the right way. Obviously, we want the hustle, we want the fundamentals, things of that nature. So, when you look at the Tiger Way, it’s running the bases, defensive situations, knowing where to set up, where to hit the cut-off man, things of that nature. It’s no different than the Dodger Way when I grew up. It showed you where you’re supposed to be set up on almost every play defensively and how you’re supposed to approach certain situations.",
          "word_count": 112
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_087",
          "text": "“So, it’s a step-by-step manual for the player, but also the coaches as a guideline. That’s the best way I can explain it.”",
          "html": "“So, it’s a step-by-step manual for the player, but also the coaches as a guideline. That’s the best way I can explain it.”",
          "word_count": 23
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_088",
          "text": "Avila chuckles.",
          "html": "Avila chuckles.",
          "word_count": 2
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_089",
          "text": "“It’s not like a quote or a phrase or anything like that, you know? If that’s what you’re asking.”",
          "html": "“It’s not like a quote or a phrase or anything like that, you know? If that’s what you’re asking.”",
          "word_count": 19
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_090",
          "text": "It’s not. I ask: “Do you guys have the manual? Can I see it?”",
          "html": "It’s not. I ask: “Do you guys have the manual? Can I see it?”",
          "word_count": 14
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_091",
          "text": "“It’s in the computer. No. It’s ours.”",
          "html": "“It’s in the computer. No. It’s ours.”",
          "word_count": 7
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_092",
          "text": "“There are people in the organization that have not heard anything about this. I ask them, ‘Hey, what’s the status of the Tiger Way—has this been done?’ They say they have no idea what this is. So, you’re saying that it’s in the computer. Any kind of proof this has been done would probably be helpful in disputing those claims, I guess.”",
          "html": "“There are people in the organization that have not heard anything about this. I ask them, ‘Hey, what’s the status of the Tiger Way—has this been done?’ They say they have no idea what this is. So, you’re saying that it’s in the computer. Any kind of proof this has been done would probably be helpful in disputing those claims, I guess.”",
          "word_count": 62
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_093",
          "text": "“I’m not going to get into that if you’re going that direction.”",
          "html": "“I’m not going to get into that if you’re going that direction.”",
          "word_count": 12
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_094",
          "text": "“But you are saying that it has been done?”",
          "html": "“But you are saying that it has been done?”",
          "word_count": 9
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_095",
          "text": "“Yeah. But as I told you, it’s always a work in progress.”",
          "html": "“Yeah. But as I told you, it’s always a work in progress.”",
          "word_count": 12
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_096",
          "text": "I connect with a minor-league manager after the media session.",
          "html": "I connect with a minor-league manager after the media session.",
          "word_count": 10
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_097",
          "text": "“I asked Al to show me the Tiger Way tonight.”",
          "html": "“I asked Al to show me the Tiger Way tonight.”",
          "word_count": 10
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_098",
          "text": "“And u probably got a confused look.”",
          "html": "“And u probably got a confused look.”",
          "word_count": 7
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_099",
          "text": "“Brutally awkward. Stumbling and bumbling about what it is, and then he says he won’t show it to me.”",
          "html": "“Brutally awkward. Stumbling and bumbling about what it is, and then he says he won’t show it to me.”",
          "word_count": 19
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_100",
          "text": "The manager laughs. “Because it doesn’t exist!”",
          "html": "The manager laughs. “Because it doesn’t exist!”",
          "word_count": 7
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_101",
          "text": "Five years earlier, I proudly introduced myself to Ken Rosenthal in this lobby. Met Scott Boras here. Back then, I wanted my phone to flash 24/7/365 with “important people,” influential dealmakers and the ilk.",
          "html": "Five years earlier, I proudly introduced myself to Ken Rosenthal in this lobby. Met Scott Boras here. Back then, I wanted my phone to flash 24/7/365 with “important people,” influential dealmakers and the ilk.",
          "word_count": 34
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_102",
          "text": "Now, I just want Rosenthal to walk up to me like he did a couple years ago in K.C., coming over to say hello, shaking my hand in the clubhouse and complimenting me on the “heck of a story” I wrote the previous weekend about the Tigers’ collapse.",
          "html": "Now, I just want Rosenthal to walk up to me like he did a couple years ago in K.C., coming over to say hello, shaking my hand in the clubhouse and complimenting me on the “heck of a story” I wrote the previous weekend about the Tigers’ collapse.",
          "word_count": 48
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_103",
          "text": "I want to feel like Fenech again—not an unethical schmuck, uncomfortable in his own skin and shying away from folks like Rosenthal. Right now, we’re on opposite hotel escalators, and I keep my head down. I raise it long enough to catch a stray glance from baseball’s No. 1 National Guy. No acknowledgment. Ken—like everybody else these days—looks at me like I’m a ghost.",
          "html": "I want to feel like Fenech again—not an unethical schmuck, uncomfortable in his own skin and shying away from folks like Rosenthal. Right now, we’re on opposite hotel escalators, and I keep my head down. I raise it long enough to catch a stray glance from baseball’s No. 1 National Guy. No acknowledgment. Ken—like everybody else these days—looks at me like I’m a ghost.",
          "word_count": 64
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_104",
          "text": "December 11—Bright and early, the annual managers’ buffet brunch.",
          "html": "<em>December 11</em>—Bright and early, the annual managers’ buffet brunch.",
          "word_count": 9
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_105",
          "text": "American League skippers crowd into a ballroom, sip coffee with the local Ball Writers and take a class yearbook-style photo.",
          "html": "American League skippers crowd into a ballroom, sip coffee with the local Ball Writers and take a class yearbook-style photo.",
          "word_count": 20
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_106",
          "text": "At our table, it’s Ron Gardenhire, the Tiger Beat and Tiger PR (Ron Colangelo, media relations director Chad Crunk and another staffer). There’s an empty seat between Gardenhire and me. He leans over and asks, “I thought you were moving to the Pistons?”",
          "html": "At our table, it’s Ron Gardenhire, the Tiger Beat and Tiger PR (Ron Colangelo, media relations director Chad Crunk and another staffer). There’s an empty seat between Gardenhire and me. He leans over and asks, “I thought you were moving to the Pistons?”",
          "word_count": 43
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_107",
          "text": "“Where did you hear that?”",
          "html": "“Where did you hear that?”",
          "word_count": 5
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_108",
          "text": "“It’s all over the Internet.”",
          "html": "“It’s all over the Internet.”",
          "word_count": 5
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_109",
          "text": "Gardy doesn’t know not to joke with me like that—I have PTSD from being all over the Internet for five years. Furiously scrolling through Twitter, I can’t find anything. I think he’s pulling my leg—but clearly, Tiger Guys have been talking in the suite.",
          "html": "Gardy doesn’t know not to joke with me like that—I have PTSD from being all over the Internet for five years. Furiously scrolling through Twitter, I can’t find anything. I think he’s pulling my leg—but clearly, Tiger Guys have been talking in the suite.",
          "word_count": 44
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_110",
          "text": "4:50 P.M.—PR sends an alert ten minutes before today’s media session: “We are pushing Al’s session back. Please be on standby.”",
          "html": "4:50 P.M.—PR sends an alert ten minutes before today’s media session: “We are pushing Al’s session back. Please be on standby.”",
          "word_count": 21
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_111",
          "text": "I bug Deep Throat again during his vacation. He’s been my safety net for years, but I’m wondering if he’s turned on me, too. “Have you heard the length of Al’s contract?” Deep Throat: “Will be happy to talk after vacation is done.”",
          "html": "I bug Deep Throat again during his vacation. He’s been my safety net for years, but I’m wondering if he’s turned on me, too. “Have you heard the length of Al’s contract?” Deep Throat: “Will be happy to talk after vacation is done.”",
          "word_count": 43
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_112",
          "text": "“You’re a jerk.”",
          "html": "“You’re a jerk.”",
          "word_count": 3
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_113",
          "text": "Deep Throat: “You’re a jerk. I told you on the phone I was headed out of the country and wasn’t going to be any help. Quit bugging me with this shit.”",
          "html": "Deep Throat: “You’re a jerk. I told you on the phone I was headed out of the country and wasn’t going to be any help. Quit bugging me with this shit.”",
          "word_count": 31
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_114",
          "text": "A day after pressing Avila on the Tiger Way, I contemplate more wartime reporting.",
          "html": "A day after pressing Avila on the Tiger Way, I contemplate more wartime reporting.",
          "word_count": 14
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_115",
          "text": "Surveying more sources, I ask if it’s fair game to ask about (and report on) the length of the contract extension Avila signed last summer.",
          "html": "Surveying more sources, I ask if it’s fair game to ask about (and report on) the length of the contract extension Avila signed last summer.",
          "word_count": 25
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_116",
          "text": "Pedro Gomez says so: “If I’m a fan, that’s something I’d like to know. Why the secret?”",
          "html": "Pedro Gomez says so: “If I’m a fan, that’s something I’d like to know. Why the secret?”",
          "word_count": 17
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_117",
          "text": "I decide to let things lie for the night. I poke out a story in my room and head down to the Seaport Ballroom, where the Professional Baseball Scouts’ Foundation banquet is being held. Kristie Ackert is there.",
          "html": "I decide to let things lie for the night. I poke out a story in my room and head down to the Seaport Ballroom, where the Professional Baseball Scouts’ Foundation banquet is being held. Kristie Ackert is there.",
          "word_count": 38
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_118",
          "text": "“Free drinks.”",
          "html": "“Free drinks.”",
          "word_count": 2
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_119",
          "text": "“Get me a glass of red.”",
          "html": "“Get me a glass of red.”",
          "word_count": 6
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_120",
          "text": "It’s waiting when I get there. Dinner program is under way. I sneak into an open seat at a front-row table. Kristie’s boyfriend asks about the book. “Is it a bridge-burning book?”",
          "html": "It’s waiting when I get there. Dinner program is under way. I sneak into an open seat at a front-row table. Kristie’s boyfriend asks about the book. “Is it a bridge-burning book?”",
          "word_count": 32
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_121",
          "text": "Poking my head into the lobby bar after the scouts’ banquet, I still can’t escape the Astros and Old Pal. Industry scuttlebutt remains fixated on an unfolding cheating scandal involving Houston’s 2017 World Series team—sign-stealing using cameras and trash can banging to tip off hitters.",
          "html": "Poking my head into the lobby bar after the scouts’ banquet, I still can’t escape the Astros and Old Pal. Industry scuttlebutt remains fixated on an unfolding cheating scandal involving Houston’s 2017 World Series team—sign-stealing using cameras and trash can banging to tip off hitters.",
          "word_count": 45
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_122",
          "text": "The irony isn’t lost on me: while I’m being called “unethical” by Justin Verlander, his team was cheating their way to a championship. Within weeks, MLB’s investigation will cost three managers their jobs, including Houston’s A.J. Hinch.",
          "html": "The irony isn’t lost on me: while I’m being called “unethical” by Justin Verlander, his team was cheating their way to a championship. Within weeks, MLB’s investigation will cost three managers their jobs, including Houston’s A.J. Hinch.",
          "word_count": 37
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_123",
          "text": "I swore I wouldn’t stay in the lobby for more than one, but here I am, holding a third drink.",
          "html": "I swore I wouldn’t stay in the lobby for more than one, but here I am, holding a third drink.",
          "word_count": 20
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_124",
          "text": "Later, I step out for a cigarette, and the bizarro worlds I’ve been living in this week collide. Al Avila strolls through the lobby with a drink. Odds are, it’s not his first or second. We’re in the same boat—except I’ve got smokes. So, we come together, again. As uneasy as I may feel these days in public, I’m always comfortable around Al. Even now. Even after grilling him in the team suite.",
          "html": "Later, I step out for a cigarette, and the bizarro worlds I’ve been living in this week collide. Al Avila strolls through the lobby with a drink. Odds are, it’s not his first or second. We’re in the same boat—except I’ve got smokes. So, we come together, again. As uneasy as I may feel these days in public, I’m always comfortable around Al. Even now. Even after grilling him in the team suite.",
          "word_count": 73
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_125",
          "text": "One night we decided that, if we crossed paths in the cosmos at the right time and place, we could have grown up best friends. Al even invoked divine intervention.",
          "html": "One night we decided that, if we crossed paths in the cosmos at the right time and place, we could have grown up best friends. Al even invoked divine intervention.",
          "word_count": 30
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_126",
          "text": "“This was His way of bringing us together.”",
          "html": "“This was His way of bringing us together.”",
          "word_count": 8
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_127",
          "text": "December 12—Five years ago, I’d contact sources like a mad man, building my baseball spider web from brunch time until the lobby bar. Now, I can’t get out of here soon enough.",
          "html": "<em>December 12</em>—Five years ago, I’d contact sources like a mad man, building my baseball spider web from brunch time until the lobby bar. Now, I can’t get out of here soon enough.",
          "word_count": 32
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_128",
          "text": "Unfortunately, I can’t escape until the Rule 5 draft is complete. Detroit selects pitcher Rony García from the Yankees, but before I can even research him, my phone explodes with Austin Romine signing news.",
          "html": "Unfortunately, I can’t escape until the Rule 5 draft is complete. Detroit selects pitcher Rony García from the Yankees, but before I can even research him, my phone explodes with Austin Romine signing news.",
          "word_count": 34
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_129",
          "text": "I spend the morning chasing contract details, texting agents, and trying to nail down figures—the usual winter meetings chaos, but without any enthusiasm.",
          "html": "I spend the morning chasing contract details, texting agents, and trying to nail down figures—the usual winter meetings chaos, but without any enthusiasm.",
          "word_count": 23
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_130",
          "text": "At the airport, I spot Tigers legal counsel John Westhoff—the same guy I saw before my first winter meetings five years ago. When small talk turns to my impending assignment change, I fake a smile: “I’m actually looking forward to it.”",
          "html": "At the airport, I spot Tigers legal counsel John Westhoff—the same guy I saw before my first winter meetings five years ago. When small talk turns to my impending assignment change, I fake a smile: “I’m actually looking forward to it.”",
          "word_count": 41
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_131",
          "text": "Flight home, I write about the Romine signing. Two years ago, he caught for the Yankees, helping ignite a brawl with Miguel Cabrera. Now he’s a Tiger. Baseball’s funny like that.",
          "html": "Flight home, I write about the Romine signing. Two years ago, he caught for the Yankees, helping ignite a brawl with Miguel Cabrera. Now he’s a Tiger. Baseball’s funny like that.",
          "word_count": 31
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_132",
          "text": "4:02 P.M.—After filing my column, I’m slapped in the face. An email lists three open jobs—mine among them. Reading it makes me sick with embarrassment.",
          "html": "4:02 P.M.—After filing my column, I’m slapped in the face. An email lists three open jobs—mine among them. Reading it makes me sick with embarrassment.",
          "word_count": 25
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_133",
          "text": "8:21 P.M.—Ron Colangelo texts a link about Pistons center Andre Drummond being a game-time decision due to an allergic reaction to an avocado.",
          "html": "8:21 P.M.—Ron Colangelo texts a link about Pistons center Andre Drummond being a game-time decision due to an allergic reaction to an avocado.",
          "word_count": 23
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_134",
          "text": "“See what awaits you…”",
          "html": "“See what awaits you…”",
          "word_count": 4
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_135",
          "text": "I can’t decide if he’s being supportive or touchdown-dancing on my grave.",
          "html": "I can’t decide if he’s being supportive or touchdown-dancing on my grave.",
          "word_count": 12
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_136",
          "text": "December 16—Deep Throat is officially back on American soil.",
          "html": "<em>December 16</em>—Deep Throat is officially back on American soil.",
          "word_count": 9
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_137",
          "text": "“Hi Anthony, thank you for letting me enjoy my trip. I got you something and that’s a heads-up the Lou (Whitaker) number retirement announcement will come as soon as tomorrow if you want a story prepared.”",
          "html": "“Hi Anthony, thank you for letting me enjoy my trip. I got you something and that’s a heads-up the Lou (Whitaker) number retirement announcement will come as soon as tomorrow if you want a story prepared.”",
          "word_count": 36
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_138",
          "text": "Deep Throat’s heard chatter about “not saying anything to Fenech.” He keeps in touch. But after the Tigers iced me out at the winter meeting, he’s keeping in touch. As are others.",
          "html": "Deep Throat’s heard chatter about “not saying anything to Fenech.” He keeps in touch. But after the Tigers iced me out at the winter meeting, he’s keeping in touch. As are others.",
          "word_count": 32
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_139",
          "text": "“How you doing?” a co-worker asks. “Hanging in there.”",
          "html": "“How you doing?” a co-worker asks. “Hanging in there.”",
          "word_count": 9
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_140",
          "text": "“Let’s catch up tonight bro!” a local TV reporter says. “You doing okay? I’m at the (expletive) Pistons tonight.”",
          "html": "“Let’s catch up tonight bro!” a local TV reporter says. “You doing okay? I’m at the (expletive) Pistons tonight.”",
          "word_count": 19
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_141",
          "text": "“Did you quit?” a former colleague asks. “Or you moving to Pistons. Sorry about the abrupt message. Just surprised to see a job posting.”",
          "html": "“Did you quit?” a former colleague asks. “Or you moving to Pistons. Sorry about the abrupt message. Just surprised to see a job posting.”",
          "word_count": 24
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_142",
          "text": "Me, too.",
          "html": "Me, too.",
          "word_count": 2
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_143",
          "text": "December 21—Deep Throat drops an early Christmas present down my chimney, tipping me off that the Tigers are signing first baseman C.J. Cron and second baseman Jonathan Schoop.",
          "html": "<em>December 21</em>—Deep Throat drops an early Christmas present down my chimney, tipping me off that the Tigers are signing first baseman C.J. Cron and second baseman Jonathan Schoop.",
          "word_count": 28
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_144",
          "text": "With the team on high alert, I can’t verify through the Tigers without exposing Deep Throat— one of my only sources left. I work the agents instead.",
          "html": "With the team on high alert, I can’t verify through the Tigers without exposing Deep Throat— one of my only sources left. I work the agents instead.",
          "word_count": 27
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_145",
          "text": "When I call Schoop’s agent, he puts me on hold and immediately leaks the news to National Guy Ken Rosenthal, who tweets it out while I’m waiting on hold. I’m not kidding. While I’m on hold. When he comes back on the line, he gives me the same information.",
          "html": "When I call Schoop’s agent, he puts me on hold and immediately leaks the news to National Guy Ken Rosenthal, who tweets it out while I’m waiting on hold. I’m not kidding. <em>While I’m on hold.</em> When he comes back on the line, he gives me the same information.",
          "word_count": 49
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_146",
          "text": "After getting beat by Rosenthal by two minutes, I manage to beat Jeff Passan by three on the Cron signing.",
          "html": "After getting beat by Rosenthal by two minutes, I manage to beat Jeff Passan by three on the Cron signing.",
          "word_count": 20
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_147",
          "text": "Not bad for a local guy who’s been told he can’t cover baseball anymore and was eating Rice Krispies Treats for breakfast.",
          "html": "Not bad for a local guy who’s been told he can’t cover baseball anymore and was eating Rice Krispies Treats for breakfast.",
          "word_count": 22
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_148",
          "text": "December 23—Word that I’m not long for the beat reaches Internet Stalker, who does the honors. He breaks the news on a burner account named after his dog—the Twitter account he’d been using to harass me has been banned.",
          "html": "<em>December 23</em>—Word that I’m not long for the beat reaches Internet Stalker, who does the honors. He breaks the news on a burner account named after his dog—the Twitter account he’d been using to harass me has been banned.",
          "word_count": 39
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_149",
          "text": "“Marlo the Mutt Scoop: The Free Press has an ad for a new Tigers beat writer. Fenech leaving. Most predictable thing ever.”",
          "html": "“Marlo the Mutt Scoop: The <em>Free Press</em> has an ad for a new Tigers beat writer. Fenech leaving. Most predictable thing ever.”",
          "word_count": 22
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_150",
          "text": "December 25—Merry Christmas!",
          "html": "<em>December 25</em>—Merry Christmas!",
          "word_count": 3
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_151",
          "text": "I receive a text from a local media friend, wondering what’s going on. He shares a bulletin from the Michigan State University sports journalism department, advertising my job: The Detroit Free Press is looking for a Tigers beat reporter.",
          "html": "I receive a text from a local media friend, wondering what’s going on. He shares a bulletin from the Michigan State University sports journalism department, advertising my job: <em>The </em>Detroit Free Press<em> is looking for a Tigers beat reporter.</em>",
          "word_count": 39
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_152",
          "text": "“Everything ok with you?”",
          "html": "“Everything ok with you?”",
          "word_count": 4
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_153",
          "text": "“Yeah, I’m not covering the Tigers anymore.”",
          "html": "“Yeah, I’m not covering the Tigers anymore.”",
          "word_count": 7
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_154",
          "text": "“Sheez. What’s next. How can I help?”",
          "html": "“Sheez. What’s next. How can I help?”",
          "word_count": 7
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_155",
          "text": "“I’m going to be covering the Pistons.”",
          "html": "“I’m going to be covering the Pistons.”",
          "word_count": 7
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_156",
          "text": "“Good Lord.”",
          "html": "“Good Lord.”",
          "word_count": 2
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_157",
          "text": "“I know.”",
          "html": "“I know.”",
          "word_count": 2
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_158",
          "text": "I’m still on the beat until the Free Press finds someone—Vince Ellis’s last day isn’t for a few weeks. Vince sends me the link for credentials to the NBA All-Star Game in Chicago.",
          "html": "I’m still on the beat until the <em>Free Press</em> finds someone—Vince Ellis’s last day isn’t for a few weeks. Vince sends me the link for credentials to the NBA All-Star Game in Chicago.",
          "word_count": 33
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_159",
          "text": "All is not calm. All is not bright.",
          "html": "All is not calm. All is not bright.",
          "word_count": 8
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_160",
          "text": "December 26—A local reporter publicly connects the dots: “So Anthony Fenech to exit the Tigers beat and switch to covering the Pistons to replace the buyout-taking Vince Ellis—and a new hire to cover in place of Fenech?”",
          "html": "<em>December 26</em>—A local reporter publicly connects the dots: “So Anthony Fenech to exit the Tigers beat and switch to covering the Pistons to replace the buyout-taking Vince Ellis—and a new hire to cover in place of Fenech?”",
          "word_count": 37
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_161",
          "text": "This lights up my phone. “Your choice or theirs?” a minor league guy asks. “Something up?” a former colleague wonders.",
          "html": "This lights up my phone. “Your choice or theirs?” a minor league guy asks. “Something up?” a former colleague wonders.",
          "word_count": 20
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_162",
          "text": "I spend the holidays ignoring calls and trying to dive into NBA sourcing. I’ve been building a new ScoopSheet (SwooshSheet), going through media guides, picking sourcing targets for the Pistons beat. Vince passed along contacts for scouts with the Heat and Nets.",
          "html": "I spend the holidays ignoring calls and trying to dive into NBA sourcing. I’ve been building a new ScoopSheet (SwooshSheet), going through media guides, picking sourcing targets for the Pistons beat. Vince passed along contacts for scouts with the Heat and Nets.",
          "word_count": 42
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_163",
          "text": "December 31—We had to put Fuzzles down today, four months shy of her 20th birthday. I was in sixth grade when we got her, a little ball of long gray hair. She always lived with Mom but stayed some weekends with me.",
          "html": "<em>December 31</em>—We had to put Fuzzles down today, four months shy of her 20th birthday. I was in sixth grade when we got her, a little ball of long gray hair. She always lived with Mom but stayed some weekends with me.",
          "word_count": 42
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_164",
          "text": "Fuzzles stopped eating a few days ago and kept sitting on the heat vents for comfort. We took her to the vet, who ran some tests. Kidney cancer.",
          "html": "Fuzzles stopped eating a few days ago and kept sitting on the heat vents for comfort. We took her to the vet, who ran some tests. Kidney cancer.",
          "word_count": 28
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_165",
          "text": "So, yeah. 2019 was a shitty year.",
          "html": "So, yeah. 2019 was a shitty year.",
          "word_count": 7
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_166",
          "text": "DETROIT, January 23, 2020—Still twisting in the wind, I’m sent today to the Tigers’ winter caravan kickoff at Comerica Park, like any year.",
          "html": "DETROIT, <em>January 23, 2020</em>—Still twisting in the wind, I’m sent today to the Tigers’ winter caravan kickoff at Comerica Park, like any year.",
          "word_count": 23
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_167",
          "text": "“You coming here today?” Ron Colangelo asks. “Great.”",
          "html": "“You coming here today?” Ron Colangelo asks. “Great.”",
          "word_count": 8
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_168",
          "text": "I wear my unconventional best—snake-skin cowboy boots. If this is the last time I see Michael Fulmer, I want it to be in Nanu’s boots—I’ve been telling Fulmer about them for years.",
          "html": "I wear my unconventional best—snake-skin cowboy boots. If this is the last time I see Michael Fulmer, I want it to be in Nanu’s boots—I’ve been telling Fulmer about them for years.",
          "word_count": 32
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_169",
          "text": "Any day could be my last day Ball Writing. My job has been offered to one person and you’re going to want to be seated for that one.",
          "html": "Any day could be my last day Ball Writing. My job has been offered to one person and you’re going to want to be seated for that one.",
          "word_count": 28
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_170",
          "text": "Jordan Zimmermann wonders why I’m here.",
          "html": "Jordan Zimmermann wonders why I’m here.",
          "word_count": 6
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_171",
          "text": "“I thought you were covering basketball?”",
          "html": "“I thought you were covering basketball?”",
          "word_count": 6
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_172",
          "text": "January 24—Covering TigerFest as a lame duck came less than 48 hours after I sat in a newsroom conference room with the first candidate to interview for my job: Ball Writing BFF Kristie Ackert.",
          "html": "<em>January 24</em>—Covering TigerFest as a lame duck came less than 48 hours after I sat in a newsroom conference room with the first candidate to interview for my job: Ball Writing BFF Kristie Ackert.",
          "word_count": 34
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_173",
          "text": "Yep. Of all the sports writers in the world, Coach Content landed on her.",
          "html": "Yep. Of all the sports writers in the world, Coach Content landed on her.",
          "word_count": 14
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_174",
          "text": "I have a “serious” question scribbled on my notepad—“I heard you like to steal M&Ms from the freezer, is that true?”—and give a serious answer when she asks: “Would you support me if I did end up taking the job?” “Absolutely,” I say. “100 percent. You’re one of my best friends and I’d want to do nothing but help you to succeed and I would love to work with you… but I’m going to be honest and I’ve told you this. I’m trying to get out of here. I’ve been trying to get out of here for a year, so I don’t want you to take the job thinking that I’m going to be here. Because I probably won’t be.”",
          "html": "I have a “serious” question scribbled on my notepad—“I heard you like to steal M&amp;Ms from the freezer, is that true?”—and give a serious answer when she asks: “Would you support me if I did end up taking the job?” “Absolutely,” I say. “100 percent. You’re one of my best friends and I’d want to do nothing but help you to succeed and I would love to work with you… but I’m going to be honest and I’ve told you this. I’m trying to get out of here. I’ve been trying to get out of here for a year, so I don’t want you to take the job thinking that I’m going to be here. Because I probably won’t be.”",
          "word_count": 120
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_175",
          "text": "The Daily News ended up offering Kristie more money to stay and our sports editor was having trouble finding someone. One of the people he contacted, a direct competitor, got in touch and wondered what was going on. “It surprised me,” he said. “I think you’re one of the best in the country.”",
          "html": "The<em> Daily News</em> ended up offering Kristie more money to stay and our sports editor was having trouble finding someone. One of the people he contacted, a direct competitor, got in touch and wondered what was going on. “It surprised me,” he said. “I think you’re one of the best in the country.”",
          "word_count": 53
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_176",
          "text": "So, I called Coach Content, that’s how serious I was, and I set up a meeting, determined to fall on the sword. I psyched him out with buzz words: Content. Engagement. Clicks.",
          "html": "So, I called Coach Content, that’s how serious I was, and I set up a meeting, determined to fall on the sword. I psyched him out with buzz words: Content. Engagement. Clicks.",
          "word_count": 32
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_177",
          "text": "It worked, and he gave me back my job.",
          "html": "It worked, and he gave me back my job.",
          "word_count": 9
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_178",
          "text": "He shared the good news at a colleague’s going-away party. For a brief second, I felt relief for the first time in Lord knows how long, like I could smile again, until he said this:",
          "html": "He shared the good news at a colleague’s going-away party. For a brief second, I felt relief for the first time in Lord knows how long, like I could smile again, until he said this:",
          "word_count": 35
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_179",
          "text": "“Don’t fuck it up.”",
          "html": "“Don’t fuck it up.”",
          "word_count": 4
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_180",
          "text": "February 25—Today, I’m in the newsroom to present my findings of the investigation story I’ve been working on since last July, when I sent Ron Colangelo to voicemail during one of Gardy’s pregame media sessions in Kansas City.",
          "html": "<em>February 25—</em>Today, I’m in the newsroom to present my findings of the investigation story I’ve been working on since last July, when I sent Ron Colangelo to voicemail during one of Gardy’s pregame media sessions in Kansas City.",
          "word_count": 38
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_181",
          "text": "“Call when you can,” he texted me.",
          "html": "“Call when you can,” he texted me.",
          "word_count": 7
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_182",
          "text": "That was the first tell.",
          "html": "That was the first tell.",
          "word_count": 5
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_183",
          "text": "I had texted him minutes earlier: a business-side scoop designed to ruin his day: “Do you have any background or a quote for when I write that two of the top ticket guys got fired?” That he responded so quickly, with a call, then a text, was unusual.",
          "html": "I had texted him minutes earlier: a business-side scoop designed to ruin his day: “Do you have any background or a quote for when I write that two of the top ticket guys got fired?” That he responded so quickly, with a call, then a text, was unusual.",
          "word_count": 48
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_184",
          "text": "As the Tigers struggled through another terrible season, my reporting eye strayed elsewhere in the organization. That morning, I heard those two executives, both closely tied to ownership, were recently dismissed.",
          "html": "As the Tigers struggled through another terrible season, my reporting eye strayed elsewhere in the organization. That morning, I heard those two executives, both closely tied to ownership, were recently dismissed.",
          "word_count": 31
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_185",
          "text": "Colangelo’s top priority is protecting ownership’s brand. He called again later, saying in so many words that there was nothing to see there. I believed him, and called the source who tipped me off, and talked to them for hours about how the people have been leaving in droves since new management was installed, and here’s why.",
          "html": "Colangelo’s top priority is protecting ownership’s brand. He called again later, saying in so many words that there was nothing to see there. I believed him, and called the source who tipped me off, and talked to them for hours about how the people have been leaving in droves since new management was installed, and here’s why.",
          "word_count": 57
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_186",
          "text": "I called people while on holiday in Malta and went to get a pizza with two Tigers folks immediately after the flight back, right around the time I started turning up the volume—two weeks before I was taken off the beat in November.",
          "html": "I called people while on holiday in Malta and went to get a pizza with two Tigers folks immediately after the flight back, right around the time I started turning up the volume—two weeks before I was taken off the beat in November.",
          "word_count": 43
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_187",
          "text": "I speak in front of six people, including the top news editor and sports editor. The investigations editor was scheduled to show up, but they announced he’s leaving just a few hours ago.",
          "html": "I speak in front of six people, including the top news editor and sports editor. The investigations editor was scheduled to show up, but they announced he’s leaving just a few hours ago.",
          "word_count": 33
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_188",
          "text": "In the meeting, I break down what I have:",
          "html": "In the meeting, I break down what I have:",
          "word_count": 9
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_189",
          "text": "“Last June, a veteran Tigers VP of ticket sales hosted a barbeque at his house to reward the ticket department for hitting their goal. The goal was met despite working under a young VP hired in February, whose leadership style has driven a mass exodus of employees. The week after the barbeque, the two veteran VPs were fired.",
          "html": "“<em>Last June, a veteran Tigers VP of ticket sales hosted a barbeque at his house to reward the ticket department for hitting their goal. The goal was met despite working under a young VP hired in February, whose leadership style has driven a mass exodus of employees. The week after the barbeque, the two veteran VPs were fired.</em>",
          "word_count": 58
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_190",
          "text": "“The firings were the Tigers’ latest effort to distance the business side from an old guard of employees who worked under Mike Ilitch. Since he died, employees lost their company pension in 2017; ticket employees work under uncertain commission pay, which has spurred legal action by one former employee; and work culture has cratered.",
          "html": "“<em>The firings were the Tigers’ latest effort to distance the business side from an old guard of employees who worked under Mike Ilitch. Since he died, employees lost their company pension in 2017; ticket employees work under uncertain commission pay, which has spurred legal action by one former employee; and work culture has cratered.</em>",
          "word_count": 54
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_191",
          "text": "“Ownership’s recent executive hires have contributed. One major hire was arrested for twice exposing himself in public and subsequently fired. And the latest VP hire has driven the ticket department into the ground. Among claims levied: The new ticket VP has allegedly asked a female employee to change into a dress before a prospective client gathering.",
          "html": "“<em>Ownership’s recent executive hires have contributed. One major hire was arrested for twice exposing himself in public and subsequently fired. And the latest VP hire has driven the ticket department into the ground. Among claims levied: The new ticket VP has allegedly asked a female employee to change into a dress before a prospective client gathering.</em>",
          "word_count": 56
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_192",
          "text": "“In total, over 70 people have left the business side over the past two seasons. Employees describe a non-diverse organization that does not value its workers.”",
          "html": "“<em>In total, over 70 people have left the business side over the past two seasons. Employees describe a non-diverse organization that does not value its workers.</em>”",
          "word_count": 26
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_193",
          "text": "They asked questions; I gave what answers I could.",
          "html": "They asked questions; I gave what answers I could.",
          "word_count": 9
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_194",
          "text": "Focus on one thing, they said. We need more. Someone willing to go on the record.",
          "html": "Focus on one thing, they said. We need more. Someone willing to go on the record.",
          "word_count": 16
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_195",
          "text": "March 3—Good news: I didn’t fuck it up. Today I make it “official-official” in the newsroom.",
          "html": "<em>March 3</em>—Good news: I didn’t fuck it up. Today I make it “official-official” in the newsroom.",
          "word_count": 16
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_196",
          "text": "I was told two weeks ago that I was back on the beat, but Boss has so far balked at sending the Ball Writer down to spring training. The backup Lions football writer remains in TigerTown.",
          "html": "I was told two weeks ago that I was back on the beat, but Boss has so far balked at sending the Ball Writer down to spring training. The backup Lions football writer remains in TigerTown.",
          "word_count": 36
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_197",
          "text": "A few days ago, he said he had a memo for me to sign, and after that, we were golden.",
          "html": "A few days ago, he said he had a memo for me to sign, and after that, we were golden.",
          "word_count": 20
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_198",
          "text": "Reading over the memo, I spot a big red flag. It says I must grow page views by 10 percent year-over-year. I ask him if I could have the union rep to give it a look. Union Rep says don’t touch it—performance-based clauses are not permitted for bargaining unit employees.",
          "html": "Reading over the memo, I spot a big red flag. It says I must grow page views by 10 percent year-over-year. I ask him if I could have the union rep to give it a look. Union Rep says don’t touch it—performance-based clauses are not permitted for bargaining unit employees.",
          "word_count": 50
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_199",
          "text": "Thwarted, he sends another memo, no gotchas about it. He offers this recent evaluation:",
          "html": "Thwarted, he sends another memo, no gotchas about it. He offers this recent evaluation:",
          "word_count": 14
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_200",
          "text": "“Anthony has shown exceptional improvement in communication and collaboration over the past month after being reassigned from the Tigers beat in November 2019.”",
          "html": "“Anthony has shown exceptional improvement in communication and collaboration over the past month after being reassigned from the Tigers beat in November 2019.”",
          "word_count": 23
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_201",
          "text": "SAN PEDRO de MACORIS, Dominican Republic, March 10—A buddy asks what I’m doing here.",
          "html": "SAN PEDRO de MACORIS, Dominican Republic, <em>March 10</em>—A buddy asks what I’m doing here.",
          "word_count": 14
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_202",
          "text": "“I got my job back.”",
          "html": "“I got my job back.”",
          "word_count": 5
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_203",
          "text": "“What????”",
          "html": "“What????”",
          "word_count": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_204",
          "text": "It’s a long story. What matters is that I’m here, where the back roads are bumpy and my driver crawls between sugarcane crops in his wife’s Subaru.",
          "html": "It’s a long story. What matters is that I’m here, where the back roads are bumpy and my driver crawls between sugarcane crops in his wife’s Subaru.",
          "word_count": 27
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_205",
          "text": "Oliver Arias, a Dominican area scout, has been my tour guide and interpreter for two days while I report from the Tigers’ academy.",
          "html": "Oliver Arias, a Dominican area scout, has been my tour guide and interpreter for two days while I report from the Tigers’ academy.",
          "word_count": 23
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_206",
          "text": "After the nightmare of 2019, being back on any assignment feels surreal. Yesterday I profiled the mystery top prospect from Cuba they sent me here to cover. Today I’m watching 80 international prospects emerge from dormitories at 9:21 A.M.",
          "html": "After the nightmare of 2019, being back on any assignment feels surreal. Yesterday I profiled the mystery top prospect from Cuba they sent me here to cover. Today I’m watching 80 international prospects emerge from dormitories at 9:21 A.M.",
          "word_count": 39
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_207",
          "text": "Two flights away from spring training, the coronavirus dominates the media cycle. Eight cases in Florida yesterday—the state’s first significant jump.",
          "html": "Two flights away from spring training, the coronavirus dominates the media cycle. Eight cases in Florida yesterday—the state’s first significant jump.",
          "word_count": 21
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_208",
          "text": "In the morning, another jump. Mom is terrified. “Are you in FL yet? Got your wipes? Don’t shake hands with anyone… Over 1,000 in U.S., 30 deaths.”",
          "html": "In the morning, another jump. Mom is terrified. “Are you in FL yet? Got your wipes? Don’t shake hands with anyone… Over 1,000 in U.S., 30 deaths.”",
          "word_count": 27
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_209",
          "text": "ATLANTA, March 11—Two-hour layover. More people wearing masks than I’ve ever seen, including bartenders. Every TV shows red breaking news ribbons: CDC: AT LEAST 1,200+ COVID-19 CASES IN U.S.",
          "html": "ATLANTA, <em>March 11</em>—Two-hour layover. More people wearing masks than I’ve ever seen, including bartenders. Every TV shows red breaking news ribbons: CDC: AT LEAST 1,200+ COVID-19 CASES IN U.S.",
          "word_count": 29
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_210",
          "text": "Messages when I land in Tampa: “When you have a min, give me a call.”—Willie Horton. “Call if you get the chance.”—Deep Throat. “Are you in Lakeland yet?”—Mom.",
          "html": "Messages when I land in Tampa: “When you have a min, give me a call.”—Willie Horton. “Call if you get the chance.”—Deep Throat. “Are you in Lakeland yet?”—Mom.",
          "word_count": 28
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_211",
          "text": "I call Mr. Horton (no answer) and talk with Deep Throat for 20 minutes on the drive, then check into the hotel and head to the bar.",
          "html": "I call Mr. Horton (no answer) and talk with Deep Throat for 20 minutes on the drive, then check into the hotel and head to the bar.",
          "word_count": 27
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_212",
          "text": "Sunny, 77 degrees, and smells like spring training. I made it to Florida for Ball Writing’s best month. Only got 14 days, let’s make the most of ‘em.",
          "html": "Sunny, 77 degrees, and smells like spring training. I made it to Florida for Ball Writing’s best month. Only got 14 days, let’s make the most of ‘em.",
          "word_count": 28
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_213",
          "text": "LAKELAND, Fla., March 12—By morning, the sports world begins to spin more slowly.",
          "html": "LAKELAND, Fla., <em>March 12</em>—By morning, the sports world begins to spin more slowly.",
          "word_count": 13
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_214",
          "text": "“Hopefully you brought your wipes,” Mom texts me. “They quarantined Pistons. They played Jazz on Saturday. The player from Jazz has the virus.”",
          "html": "“Hopefully you brought your wipes,” Mom texts me. “They quarantined Pistons. They played Jazz on Saturday. The player from Jazz has the virus.”",
          "word_count": 23
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_215",
          "text": "Two days after Utah’s All-Star center Rudy Gobert mocked questions about the pandemic, touching recorders and microphones following a press conference, he tests positive. Gobert was scratched in the lead-up to last night’s Utah-Oklahoma City game, which was soon postponed, setting off a firestorm of events.",
          "html": "Two days after Utah’s All-Star center Rudy Gobert mocked questions about the pandemic, touching recorders and microphones following a press conference, he tests positive. Gobert was scratched in the lead-up to last night’s Utah-Oklahoma City game, which was soon postponed, setting off a firestorm of events.",
          "word_count": 46
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_216",
          "text": "This morning, many in baseball forecast the same fate. “We’re always the last to act.”",
          "html": "This morning, many in baseball forecast the same fate. “We’re always the last to act.”",
          "word_count": 15
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_217",
          "text": "Me? I’m just happy to be back, even if it’s in a mask.",
          "html": "Me? I’m just happy to be back, even if it’s in a mask.",
          "word_count": 13
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_218",
          "text": "I arrive for my sixth spring training the same day as the coronavirus. I hit the ground running—there is other important news besides impending doomsday. This week was the Tigers’ open tryout, one of the few remaining in baseball.",
          "html": "I arrive for my sixth spring training the same day as the coronavirus. I hit the ground running—there is other important news besides impending doomsday. This week was the Tigers’ open tryout, one of the few remaining in baseball.",
          "word_count": 39
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_219",
          "text": "I check with a source. Nobody was signed.",
          "html": "I check with a source. Nobody was signed.",
          "word_count": 8
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_220",
          "text": "All I know right now is that it’s good to be back. Good to see the parking lot attendant whose name escapes me. “Why hello stranger!” he beams. Good to see the lobby secretary and Michele Wysocki, who last season left her job as Tigers media relations coordinator—she has tickets on the Margaritaville patio deck in right field.",
          "html": "All I know right now is that it’s good to be back. Good to see the parking lot attendant whose name escapes me. “Why hello stranger!” he beams. Good to see the lobby secretary and Michele Wysocki, who last season left her job as Tigers media relations coordinator—she has tickets on the Margaritaville patio deck in right field.",
          "word_count": 58
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_221",
          "text": "With clubhouses closed, Tigers PR facilitates interviews by request. I ask Crunk for players’ union rep Matthew Boyd and the team’s head trainer.",
          "html": "With clubhouses closed, Tigers PR facilitates interviews by request. I ask Crunk for players’ union rep Matthew Boyd and the team’s head trainer.",
          "word_count": 23
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_222",
          "text": "I go 1-for-2 in my spring debut. The trainer can’t talk, but Boyd does—speaking to reporters inside the lobby at team HQ, expressing hope that baseball won’t shut down.",
          "html": "I go 1-for-2 in my spring debut. The trainer can’t talk, but Boyd does—speaking to reporters inside the lobby at team HQ, expressing hope that baseball won’t shut down.",
          "word_count": 29
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_223",
          "text": "He stands six feet away, behind an elastic line. He’s wearing metal spikes, holding a baseball glove, planning to throw later in the outfield.",
          "html": "He stands six feet away, behind an elastic line. He’s wearing metal spikes, holding a baseball glove, planning to throw later in the outfield.",
          "word_count": 24
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_224",
          "text": "“If you get sick, you get sick. There’s so much that is out of your control. You can do what you want but you can’t go live life out of fear—that’s not what you’re supposed to do. That’s not living as you’re called to.”",
          "html": "“If you get sick, you get sick. There’s so much that is out of your control. You can do what you want but you can’t go live life out of fear—that’s not what you’re supposed to do. That’s not living as you’re called to.”",
          "word_count": 44
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_225",
          "text": "Boyd is asked if he thinks spring training will continue.",
          "html": "Boyd is asked if he thinks spring training will continue.",
          "word_count": 10
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_226",
          "text": "“I think the show is going to go on as long as it can.”",
          "html": "“I think the show is going to go on as long as it can.”",
          "word_count": 14
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_227",
          "text": "Detroit takes the field for stretch, calisthenics and batting practice.",
          "html": "Detroit takes the field for stretch, calisthenics and batting practice.",
          "word_count": 10
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_228",
          "text": "I climb over the short fence next to the dugout, where Miguel Cabrera welcomes me to camp the only way he can—he gives me the finger.",
          "html": "I climb over the short fence next to the dugout, where Miguel Cabrera welcomes me to camp the only way he can—he gives me the finger.",
          "word_count": 26
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_229",
          "text": "Miggy loosens up behind the cage, readying for batting practice. I smile and wave back.",
          "html": "Miggy loosens up behind the cage, readying for batting practice. I smile and wave back.",
          "word_count": 15
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_230",
          "text": "Teams begin pulling their scouts from the road.",
          "html": "Teams begin pulling their scouts from the road.",
          "word_count": 8
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_231",
          "text": "Rival Exec: “Multiple teams are pulling scouts: Red Sox, Angels, Cardinals, and others.”",
          "html": "Rival Exec: “Multiple teams are pulling scouts: Red Sox, Angels, Cardinals, and others.”",
          "word_count": 13
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_232",
          "text": "Adjacent to the media dining tent, former Tiger reliever Shane Greene stands outside the visitor’s clubhouse. Greene is still with Atlanta after last season’s trade. He’s as surprised as anybody that they’re playing today.",
          "html": "Adjacent to the media dining tent, former Tiger reliever Shane Greene stands outside the visitor’s clubhouse. Greene is still with Atlanta after last season’s trade. He’s as surprised as anybody that they’re playing today.",
          "word_count": 34
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_233",
          "text": "“We touch the ball on every pitch,” Greene says, spinning a ball off his fingers in slow-motion. “By just throwing the ball, players could be at risk.”",
          "html": "“We touch the ball on every pitch,” Greene says, spinning a ball off his fingers in slow-motion. “By just throwing the ball, players could be at risk.”",
          "word_count": 27
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_234",
          "text": "Having a margarita in Section 105, Wysocki texts me: “Stop by if you need a break.”",
          "html": "Having a margarita in Section 105, Wysocki texts me: “Stop by if you need a break.”",
          "word_count": 16
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_235",
          "text": "“A break or a margarita?”",
          "html": "“A break or a margarita?”",
          "word_count": 5
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_236",
          "text": "“Well, I’m not sharing mine.”",
          "html": "“Well, I’m not sharing mine.”",
          "word_count": 5
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_237",
          "text": "My days in baseball may be numbered, as well. The desk has sent six text messages and two emails so far today—and the game hasn’t even started.",
          "html": "My days in baseball may be numbered, as well. The desk has sent six text messages and two emails so far today—and the game hasn’t even started.",
          "word_count": 27
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_238",
          "text": "When it does, Víctor Reyes makes a nice running catch in left field.",
          "html": "When it does, Víctor Reyes makes a nice running catch in left field.",
          "word_count": 13
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_239",
          "text": "While the Braves and Tigers begin play, the sports world continues toward a hard stop—and speculation ensues baseball is next.",
          "html": "While the Braves and Tigers begin play, the sports world continues toward a hard stop—and speculation ensues baseball is next.",
          "word_count": 20
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_240",
          "text": "“MLB is on deck,” Deep Throat warns.",
          "html": "“MLB is on deck,” Deep Throat warns.",
          "word_count": 7
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_241",
          "text": "In the newsroom up north, the editor on duty agrees: “Start pumping out that ‘MLB is shutting down’ story. Looks like it’s inevitable.”",
          "html": "In the newsroom up north, the editor on duty agrees: “Start pumping out that ‘MLB is shutting down’ story. Looks like it’s inevitable.”",
          "word_count": 23
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_242",
          "text": "Deep Throat is on Line 1: “MLB statement at 2.”",
          "html": "Deep Throat is on Line 1: “MLB statement at 2.”",
          "word_count": 10
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_243",
          "text": "“How some teams haven’t told their guys to go home is beyond me,” one source says. “MLB blew this one hard. When the NBA suspended, it should have been immediate.”",
          "html": "“How some teams haven’t told their guys to go home is beyond me,” one source says. “MLB blew this one hard. When the NBA suspended, it should have been immediate.”",
          "word_count": 30
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_244",
          "text": "Selfishly, I’m glad it wasn’t.",
          "html": "Selfishly, I’m glad it wasn’t.",
          "word_count": 5
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_245",
          "text": "Tigers lead Braves, 2-1, bottom of the sixth.",
          "html": "Tigers lead Braves, 2-1, bottom of the sixth.",
          "word_count": 8
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_246",
          "text": "Shane Greene finishes a scoreless inning by striking out Cabrera swinging. In midseason form, Miggy appeals the checked swing to the first base umpire, who upholds strike three.",
          "html": "Shane Greene finishes a scoreless inning by striking out Cabrera swinging. In midseason form, Miggy appeals the checked swing to the first base umpire, who upholds strike three.",
          "word_count": 28
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_247",
          "text": "MLB announces it is suspending spring training and pushing back the start of the regular season by at least two weeks.",
          "html": "MLB announces it is suspending spring training and pushing back the start of the regular season by at least two weeks.",
          "word_count": 21
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_248",
          "text": "Opening Day was supposed to be March 26. Now it’s April 8, at best.",
          "html": "Opening Day was supposed to be March 26. Now it’s April 8, at best.",
          "word_count": 14
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_249",
          "text": "This game continues. Down three runs in the ninth, Hittin’ Harold Castro smacks an RBI single, and Detroit brings the tying run to the plate. With dark coronavirus clouds moving in and spring training already doomed, the crowd stirs for the last time in who knows how long.",
          "html": "This game continues. Down three runs in the ninth, Hittin’ Harold Castro smacks an RBI single, and Detroit brings the tying run to the plate. With dark coronavirus clouds moving in and spring training already doomed, the crowd stirs for the last time in who knows how long.",
          "word_count": 48
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_250",
          "text": "The rally falls short. Tigers lose.",
          "html": "The rally falls short. Tigers lose.",
          "word_count": 6
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_251",
          "text": "Postgame, Boyd addresses reporters again. Privy to private Players’ Association discussions, Boyd shares what he can about the immediate future.",
          "html": "Postgame, Boyd addresses reporters again. Privy to private Players’ Association discussions, Boyd shares what he can about the immediate future.",
          "word_count": 20
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_252",
          "text": "“I was wrong earlier. Didn’t take long for that to switch around.”",
          "html": "“I was wrong earlier. Didn’t take long for that to switch around.”",
          "word_count": 12
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_253",
          "text": "The team will stay in Lakeland until further notice. Informal, optional workouts will be conducted.",
          "html": "The team will stay in Lakeland until further notice. Informal, optional workouts will be conducted.",
          "word_count": 15
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_254",
          "text": "After Boyd speaks, Al Avila and Ron Gardenhire step in.",
          "html": "After Boyd speaks, Al Avila and Ron Gardenhire step in.",
          "word_count": 10
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_255",
          "text": "Avila wears a navy polo; a ballpoint pen hooked between buttons. The Tigers will have their facilities deep-cleaned, top-to-bottom. No positive tests so far. Gardenhire is asked how he found out—from a field-level security guard, he says, who showed him his phone.",
          "html": "Avila wears a navy polo; a ballpoint pen hooked between buttons. The Tigers will have their facilities deep-cleaned, top-to-bottom. No positive tests so far. Gardenhire is asked how he found out—from a field-level security guard, he says, who showed him his phone.",
          "word_count": 42
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_256",
          "text": "“Read this.”",
          "html": "“Read this.”",
          "word_count": 2
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_257",
          "text": "“I kinda got a game going on. So, it was different. No doubt, it was different.”",
          "html": "“I kinda got a game going on. So, it was different. No doubt, it was different.”",
          "word_count": 16
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_258",
          "text": "It’s good to see them—even if we are standing six feet apart and roped off. I stand in the back of the reporting bunch, next to a stairway that winds up to the Tigers’ front offices.",
          "html": "It’s good to see them—even if we are standing six feet apart and roped off. I stand in the back of the reporting bunch, next to a stairway that winds up to the Tigers’ front offices.",
          "word_count": 36
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_259",
          "text": "Walking behind me, Al pinches my ear.",
          "html": "Walking behind me, Al pinches my ear.",
          "word_count": 7
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_260",
          "text": "A scout friend suggests dinner before the world ends.",
          "html": "A scout friend suggests dinner before the world ends.",
          "word_count": 9
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_261",
          "text": "Larry the press box attendant is gone, and the computer screen is asleep. I’ve been the last man hanging for almost half an hour now—no lights, mini fridge locked, sun shading a stadium that might not get much use for a while.",
          "html": "Larry the press box attendant is gone, and the computer screen is asleep. I’ve been the last man hanging for almost half an hour now—no lights, mini fridge locked, sun shading a stadium that might not get much use for a while.",
          "word_count": 42
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_262",
          "text": "I don’t write. Just sit and think.",
          "html": "I don’t write. Just sit and think.",
          "word_count": 7
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_263",
          "text": "After years of filing quickly to meet print deadlines and feed the web and promptly leave the park, I can’t bring myself to do anything but sit here and think about the good ol’ days. Sometimes, I smile.",
          "html": "After years of filing quickly to meet print deadlines and feed the web and promptly leave the park, I can’t bring myself to do anything but sit here and think about the good ol’ days. Sometimes, I smile.",
          "word_count": 38
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_264",
          "text": "I think about my first time here, a problem child for PR even back then. Left unattended at spring training in 2014 as an emergency fill-in for Seamhead John Lowe, I took a picture of a gag posted in the clubhouse—a picture of backup catcher Bryan Holaday in a stars-and-stripes women’s one-piece photoshopped into a mock Sports Illustrated swimsuit cover.",
          "html": "I think about my first time here, a problem child for PR even back then. Left unattended at spring training in 2014 as an emergency fill-in for Seamhead John Lowe, I took a picture of a gag posted in the clubhouse—a picture of backup catcher Bryan Holaday in a stars-and-stripes women’s one-piece photoshopped into a mock <em>Sports Illustrated</em> swimsuit cover.",
          "word_count": 60
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_265",
          "text": "Of course I tweeted it, before Crunk pulled me outside and asked me to delete it—and the picture from my phone.",
          "html": "Of course I tweeted it, before Crunk pulled me outside and asked me to delete it—and the picture from my phone.",
          "word_count": 21
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_266",
          "text": "I was thrown into the Ball Writing fire when the Tigers were blindsided by an injury to Jose Iglesias, the young dynamo defender at shortstop, who was forecast to miss many months—if not the season—with a tear of the patella tendon.",
          "html": "I was thrown into the Ball Writing fire when the Tigers were blindsided by an injury to Jose Iglesias, the young dynamo defender at shortstop, who was forecast to miss many months—if not the season—with a tear of the patella tendon.",
          "word_count": 41
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_267",
          "text": "Five years since then. How would I break the news if the shortstop goes down now?",
          "html": "Five years since then. How would I break the news if the shortstop goes down now?",
          "word_count": 16
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_268",
          "text": "And when I first met Víctor Martínez that week in 2014. He called me “minor league” back then, and I worked hard on our relationship. A year later, my first covering the team in 2015, he was struggling early, hitting .240-something with only four extra-base hits.",
          "html": "And when I first met Víctor Martínez that week in 2014. He called me “minor league” back then, and I worked hard on our relationship. A year later, my first covering the team in 2015, he was struggling early, hitting .240-something with only four extra-base hits.",
          "word_count": 46
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_269",
          "text": "One night, the Tigers lost a tough one in extra innings, and after reporters from his scrum scattered, Víctor called me back.",
          "html": "One night, the Tigers lost a tough one in extra innings, and after reporters from his scrum scattered, Víctor called me back.",
          "word_count": 22
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_270",
          "text": "“Hey, Anthony…”",
          "html": "“Hey, Anthony…”",
          "word_count": 2
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_271",
          "text": "With a backpack on, turning away from his locker, he reached out to me for a fist bump. I complied, and it made me feel good as a young reporter—he gave me a sign of respect. Then he walked off through the clubhouse manager’s office and out the door. I think about how I’ll never talk to Víctor again.",
          "html": "With a backpack on, turning away from his locker, he reached out to me for a fist bump. I complied, and it made me feel good as a young reporter—he gave me a sign of respect. Then he walked off through the clubhouse manager’s office and out the door. I think about how I’ll never talk to Víctor again.",
          "word_count": 59
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_272",
          "text": "I continue to sit in the Joker Marchant Stadium press box, trying to imagine what the stadium looked like before. When there weren’t seats in right, no Margaritaville porch, just a few tall palm trees and green netting to catch homers and protect reporters and others outside the clubhouse from getting blistered with foul balls.",
          "html": "I continue to sit in the Joker Marchant Stadium press box, trying to imagine what the stadium looked like before. When there weren’t seats in right, no Margaritaville porch, just a few tall palm trees and green netting to catch homers and protect reporters and others outside the clubhouse from getting blistered with foul balls.",
          "word_count": 55
        },
        {
          "id": "p_ch25_273",
          "text": "I strain to see it. Back when there were black chain-link picnic tables out there, the kind you could stick your fingers into, where I once interviewed my favorite baseball player growing up and got razzed by Jim Leyland and spent the doe-eyed days of my cub reporting youth. A place far in the fantasy of the past, so far away from the reality of now, where I’m afraid to leave the press box because I don’t think I’ll ever be back.",
          "html": "I strain to see it. Back when there were black chain-link picnic tables out there, the kind you could stick your fingers into, where I once interviewed my favorite baseball player growing up and got razzed by Jim Leyland and spent the doe-eyed days of my cub reporting youth. A place far in the fantasy of the past, so far away from the reality of now, where I’m afraid to leave the press box because I don’t think I’ll ever be back.",
          "word_count": 82
        }
